{"parentUuid":"66e84af7-c646-43b7-ad74-74425943b2cd","isSidechain":true,"userType":"external","cwd":"/app/workspace/data","sessionId":"38c7d341-6530-47d7-8864-d8ab21466574","version":"2.1.19","gitBranch":"","agentId":"a2ead08","slug":"adaptive-exploring-penguin","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_vrtx_01SWoqaCntSJHcEf1h4Qv3ZE","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Google ClusterData 2011-2 schema task event job event columns\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"cluster-data/ClusterData2011_2.md at master · google/cluster-data\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/cluster-data/blob/master/ClusterData2011_2.md\"},{\"title\":\"Analysis and Clustering of Workload in Google\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1501.01426\"},{\"title\":\"Google Cluster Trace Dataset Overview\",\"url\":\"https://www.emergentmind.com/topics/google-cluster-trace-dataset\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Analysis and Clustering of Workload in Google Cluster Trace based on Resource Usage\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/270593953_Analysis_and_Clustering_of_Workload_in_Google_Cluster_Trace_based_on_Resource_Usage\"},{\"title\":\"Google cluster-usage traces: format + schema\",\"url\":\"https://t1.daumcdn.net/cfile/tistory/26542633597592552C\"},{\"title\":\"First Steps Exploring the Google Cluster dataset with iPython | Mark Stillwell\",\"url\":\"https://stillwell.me/~mark/post/first-steps-exploring-the-google-cluster-dataset-with-ipython/\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - tommycarpi/py-tracy: Tool to analyse the Google's traces 'clusterdata-2011-2' for both job_events and task_events.\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/tommycarpi/py-tracy\"},{\"title\":\"Google Cluster Usage Traces | PDF | Computer Data Storage | Scheduling (Computing)\",\"url\":\"https://www.scribd.com/document/901116490/Google-Cluster-Usage-Traces\"},{\"title\":\"Google cluster-usage traces: format + schema Charles Reiss, John Wilkes\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/profile/Auday-Al-Dulaimy/post/Are-there-any-datasets-for-cloudSim/attachment/59d61de379197b807797be3e/AS:273823268573184@1442295962733/download/Google+cluster+usage+traces.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"google_runtime_data: 11409 Samples of Jobs of Google ClusterData 2011 traces in carlonlv/DataCenterSim: Simulations for Data Centers\",\"url\":\"https://rdrr.io/github/carlonlv/DataCenterSim/man/google_runtime_data.html\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about the Google ClusterData 2011-2 schema for task event and job event columns:\n\n## Task Event Columns\n\nThe task event CSV files contain the fields: 'time', 'missing info', 'job ID', 'task index', 'machine_id', 'event type', 'user', 'scheduling class', 'priority', 'cpu request', 'memory request', 'disk space request', 'different machines restriction'.\n\nThe Task Events Table is represented by thirteen columns which include fields such as time stamp, missing information, index of tasks, event type, priority of a task.\n\n## Job Event Columns\n\nJob event fields include 'time', 'missing info', 'job ID', 'task index', 'machine_id', 'event type', 'user', 'scheduling class', 'priority', 'cpu request', 'memory request', 'disk space request', 'different machines restriction'.\n\n## Event Types\n\nThere are basically two types of events: ones that affect the scheduling state (e.g., a job is submitted, or it gets scheduled and becomes runnable, or its resource requests are updated), and ones that reflect state changes of a task (e.g., the task exits). Each job and task event has a value representing the type of event.\n\nFor the official schema details, the trace is described in the trace-data v2.1 format + schema document, available in the GitHub repository for Google's ClusterData.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"0d51615b-8d72-43ce-bf77-72e950383995","timestamp":"2026-01-29T06:37:26.675Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"66e84af7-c646-43b