{"parentUuid":"7ffaca37-ac68-42d2-bf4c-5e49171d2fe3","isSidechain":true,"userType":"external","cwd":"/app/workspace/data","sessionId":"38c7d341-6530-47d7-8864-d8ab21466574","version":"2.1.19","gitBranch":"","agentId":"a2ead08","slug":"adaptive-exploring-penguin","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_vrtx_01Naio9bEEZVT7t23UVmjk8R","type":"tool_result","content":"# Google Cluster Dataset Schema\n\nBased on the document, here's the schema information for the task-related events:\n\n## Task Event Columns\n\nAccording to the code, task event CSV files contain these fields:\n\n\"'time', 'missing info', 'job ID', 'task index', 'machine_id', 'event type', 'user', 'scheduling class', 'priority', 'cpu request', 'memory request', 'disk space request', 'different machines restriction'\"\n\nThe document notes that the most relevant fields for analysis are time, event type, CPU request, and memory request. The job ID and task index are needed to track task evolution over time.\n\n## Machine Event Columns\n\nMachine event files include:\n\n\"'time', 'machine ID', 'event type', 'platform ID', 'cpu capacity', 'memory capacity'\"\n\nEvent types indicate whether a machine was added (0), removed (1), or updated (2).\n\n## Task Usage Columns\n\nTask usage measurements contain nineteen fields including:\n\n\"'start time', 'end time', 'job id', 'task index', 'machine id', 'mean CPU usage', 'canonical memory usage', 'assigned memory', 'unmapped page cache memory usage', 'page cache memory usage', 'maximum memory usage'\"\n\nThe documentation recommends using mean CPU usage and canonical memory usage for modeling purposes."}]},"uuid":"30d81e0a-e5a4-4279-b688-78ae5f81a271","timestamp":"2026-01-29T06:37:54.009Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"7ffaca37-ac68-42d2-bf4c-5e49171d2fe3"}
