{"parentUuid":"ce38706e-7dde-4a7a-bbd2-7d874931cafe","isSidechain":true,"userType":"external","cwd":"/app/workspace/data","sessionId":"38c7d341-6530-47d7-8864-d8ab21466574","version":"2.1.19","gitBranch":"","agentId":"a2ead08","slug":"adaptive-exploring-penguin","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_vrtx_01UCRDVxBb8bjJtfnBW5tFGn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have both the data samples and information from the web sources. Let me create a comprehensive summary:\n\n## Summary: Data Schema Extraction\n\nBased on my analysis of the PDF file and the actual CSV data files in the `/app/workspace/data/` directory, combined with official documentation from the Google ClusterData repository, here is the extracted schema information:\n\n### Task Event Table Schema\n\n**File Location:** `/app/workspace/data/task_events/part-00001-of-00500.csv.gz`\n**Total Columns:** 13\n\n| Column # | Column Name | Data Type | Description |\n|----------|------------|-----------|-------------|\n| 1 | Time | Integer (uint64) | Timestamp in seconds since the start of data collection (May 1, 2011, 19:00 EDT) |\n| 2 | Missing Info | String | Flag indicating whether any information is missing from this record (typically empty if complete) |\n| 3 | Job ID | Integer (uint64) | Unique 64-bit identifier for the job to which this task belongs |\n| 4 | Task Index | Integer | Sequential index/identifier of the task within the job |\n| 5 | Machine ID | Integer (uint64) | Unique 64-bit identifier of the machine where the task runs (can be empty) |\n| 6 | Event Type | Integer | Type of event (0=submit, 1=schedule, 2=evict, 3=fail, 4=finish, 5=kill, 6=lost, 7=wait for re-queueing, 8=remove, 9=update pending resources, 10=update running resources) |\n| 7 | User | String (Base64-encoded hash) | Anonymized hash identifier of the user who submitted the job |\n| 8 | Scheduling Class | Integer | Priority classification for scheduling (0-low priority, 1=standard, 2=batch) |\n| 9 | Priority | Integer | Priority level (0-11 inclusive; 0-1 are free priorities, 9-11 are production priorities, 12 is monitoring) |\n| 10 | CPU Request | Float | Normalized CPU cores requested for this task (0.0-1.0 scale, relative to machine capacity) |\n| 11 | Memory Request | Float | Normalized memory requested for this task (0.0-1.0 scale, relative to machine capacity) |\n| 12 | Disk Space Request | Float | Normalized disk space requested for this task (0.0-1.0 scale) |\n| 13 | Different Machines Restriction | Integer | Boolean flag (0/1) indicating if task has constraint to run on a different machine |\n\n---\n\n### Job Event Table Schema\n\n**File Location:** `/app/workspace/data/job_events/part-00001-of-00500.csv.gz`\n**Total Columns:** 8\n\n| Column # | Column Name | Data Type | Description |\n|----------|------------|-----------|-------------|\n| 1 | Time | Integer (uint64) | Timestamp in seconds since the start of data collection |\n| 2 | Missing Info | String | Flag indicating whether any information is missing from this record |\n| 3 | Job ID | Integer (uint64) | Unique 64-bit identifier for the job |\n| 4 | Event Type | Integer | Type of job event (0=submit, 1=schedule, 2=evict, 3=fail, 4=finish, 5=kill, 6=lost, 7=wait for re-queueing, 8=remove, 9=update pending resources, 10=update running resources) |\n| 5 | User | String (Base64-encoded hash) | Anonymized hash identifier of the user/account that submitted the job |\n| 6 | Scheduling Class | Integer | Priority classification for scheduling (0=low priority, 1=standard, 2=batch) |\n| 7 | Job Name Hash | String (Base64-encoded hash) | Anonymized hash of the job name or identifier |\n| 8 | Logical Job Name Hash | String (Base64-encoded hash) | Anonymized hash of the logical job grouping/family name |\n\n---\n\n### Key Notes on Data Types and Values:\n\n**Event Types** (applies to both tables):\n- 0: SUBMIT - Job/task submitted\n- 1: SCHEDULE - Job/task scheduled to run  \n- 2: EVICT - Job/task evicted from machine\n- 3: FAIL - Job/task failed\n- 4: FINISH - Job/task completed successfully\n- 5: KILL - Job/task killed\n- 6: LOST - Job/task lost\n- 7: WAIT_FOR_RE_QUEUEING - Job/task waiting to be re-queued\n- 8: REMOVE - Job/task removed\n- 9: UPDATE_PENDING_RESOURCES - Pending resource request updated\n- 10: UPDATE_RUNNING_RESOURCES - Running resource request updated\n\n**Normalized Resource Values:** CPU, Memory, and Disk values are normalized floats (0.0-1.0) relative to the machine capacity, making them comparable across heterogeneous hardware.\n\n**Priority Ranges:**\n- 0-1: Free priorities (non-critical batch work)\n- 2-8: Normal priorities\n- 9-11: Production priorities (critical workloads)\n- 12: Monitoring priority\n\n**Missing Data Notes:** According to the documentation, approximately 0.013% of task events and 0.0008% of job events have non-empty missing info fields.\n\n---\n\n### File References:\n\nThe actual data files are located at:\n- Task Events: `/app/workspace/data/task_events/part-00001-of-00500.csv.gz` (and 499 other partitions)\n- Job Events: `/app/workspace/data/job_events/part-00001-of-00500.csv.gz` (and 499 other partitions)\n\nThe PDF file at `/app/workspace/data/format.pdf` contains the official Google ClusterData v2.1 format and schema documentation (although heavily compressed and difficult to extract directly).\n\n---\n\nSources:\n- [Google Cluster Data - GitHub Repository](https://github.com/google/cluster-data/blob/master/ClusterData2011_2.md)\n- [First Steps Exploring the Google Cluster dataset](https://stillwell.me/~mark/post/first-steps-exploring-the-google-cluster-dataset-with-ipython/)\n- [Google Cluster Trace Dataset Overview](https://www.emergentmind.com/topics/google-cluster-trace-dataset)"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1277,"cache_read_input_tokens":55311,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1277,"ephemeral_1h_input